# The octoflow-gate release (https://github.com/DavidSiegl/octoflow-gate/releases) that judges this repository's
# changes, as ci/fetch-gate.sh reads it: one line, the release's version and the sha256 of its
# octoflow-gate-<version>.tar.gz, as the release's .sha256 asset gives it. A quality build reads this file from the main
# commit it judges by, any other build from its own tree (the Jenkinsfile's Gate stage). Raise it to a new release
# only after that release exists and its downloaded tarball has passed `sha256sum -c`; lower it to roll back to an
# earlier one. The release named here must read this commit's gate.toml, which refuses keys it does not know.
